{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport bisect\nimport array\n\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\na = array.array('L', map(int, input().split()))\na1, a2 = array.array('L'), array.array('L')\nhalf = n // 2\n\ndef dfs_left(pos, total):\n    if pos == half:\n        a1.append(total)\n        return\n    dfs_left(pos + 1, (total + a[pos]) % m)\n    dfs_left(pos + 1, total)\n\ndef dfs_right(pos, total):\n    if pos == n:\n        a2.append(total)\n        return\n    dfs_right(pos + 1, (total + a[pos]) % m)\n    dfs_right(pos + 1, total)\n\ndfs_left(0, 0)\ndfs_right(half, 0)\n\na1_unique = sorted(set(a1))\nmax_sum = 0\n\nfor second_half_val in a2:\n    target = m - second_half_val\n    left_idx = bisect.bisect_left(a1_unique, target)\n    if left_idx > 0:\n        candidate = a1_unique[left_idx - 1] + second_half_val\n        if candidate > max_sum:\n            max_sum = candidate\n\nprint(max_sum)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <set>\n#include <array>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m;\n    std::cin >> n >> m;\n    \n    std::vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        std::cin >> a[i];\n    }\n    \n    std::vector<long long> a1, a2;\n    int half = n / 2;\n    \n    // DFS for left half\n    std::function<void(int, long long)> dfs_left = [&](int pos, long long total) {\n        if (pos == half) {\n            a1.push_back(total % m);\n            return;\n        }\n        dfs_left(pos + 1, (total + a[pos]) % m);\n        dfs_left(pos + 1, total);\n    };\n    \n    // DFS for right half\n    std::function<void(int, long long)> dfs_right = [&](int pos, long long total) {\n        if (pos == n) {\n            a2.push_back(total % m);\n            return;\n        }\n        dfs_right(pos + 1, (total + a[pos]) % m);\n        dfs_right(pos + 1, total);\n    };\n    \n    dfs_left(0, 0);\n    dfs_right(half, 0);\n    \n    std::set<long long> a1_set(a1.begin(), a1.end());\n    std::vector<long long> a1_unique(a1_set.begin(), a1_set.end());\n    std::sort(a1_unique.begin(), a1_unique.end());\n    \n    long long max_sum = 0;\n    \n    for (long long second_half_val : a2) {\n        long long target = m - second_half_val;\n        auto left_idx = std::lower_bound(a1_unique.begin(), a1_unique.end(), target);\n        \n        if (left_idx != a1_unique.begin()) {\n            long long candidate = *(left_idx - 1) + second_half_val;\n            if (candidate > max_sum) {\n                max_sum = candidate;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    std::cout << max_sum << std::endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00010942813969450071, -2.861018856492592e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.729855441430118e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00011431517486926168, -4.768370445162873e-07, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.00441255746409297, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.3841855067985307e